    "body": "## Problem\r\n\r\nThere is no documentation for the metatable operations for `lpeg.Pattern`s.\r\n\r\nExample from `:h Pattern:match()`:\r\n```lua\r\nlocal pattern = lpeg.R('az') ^ 1 * -1\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\n\r\nCopy documentation from <https://www.inf.puc-rio.br/~roberto/lpeg/>, modifying it slightly to not refer to \"the original PEG notation\".\r\n\r\nAdd as help tags both the metatable methods (e.g. `Pattern:__add()`), and a description of the operation (e.g. `pattern-choice`).\r\n",
    "closed_at": null,
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "I am not exactly sure how to handle the second help tag name (e.g. `pattern-choice`), since there are two approaches I can think of:\r\n\r\n1. Someone writing an lpeg grammar, wanting to know how they can do some operation (e.g. I want to match `pattern1` or `pattern2`). This would be better discovered using e.g. `pattern-choice`.\r\n2. Someone reading an lpeg grammar, wanting to know what this operation does (e.g. `pattern1 + pattern2`). This would be better discovered using e.g. `pattern-add`.\r\n\r\nWould the second case be sufficiently covered by the metatable function tag? (e.g. `Pattern:__add()`)\r\nShould I add both `pattern-add` and `pattern-choice`?",
            "created_at": "2026-08-26T16:43:46Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/41511#issuecomment-5428214481",
            "id": 5428214481,
